crypto/tls: offer ECDHE_ECDSA suites before ECDHE_RSA suites

Go fixes the order of the cipher suites a client offers and interleaves
ECDSA and RSA suites (ECDSA-AES-128, RSA-AES-128, ECDSA-AES-256,
RSA-AES-256), whatever the order of Config.CipherSuites. gemSpec_Krypt
A_17124-03 (item 3) and A_17094-02 require TLS clients in the German
health care network to offer TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 and
TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 before any RSA suite.

If Config.CipherSuites is set, as it must be in that network, which
allows only some suites, a client now offers its ECDHE_ECDSA suites
before its ECDHE_RSA suites of the same kind (AEAD, CBC, ...); the
order is otherwise Go's. Without Config.CipherSuites, the default order
is unchanged, so the recorded handshake tests keep their ClientHello.
Servers are not changed: they choose the certificate first, and the
suite must match its key.

ivory: P7, profile kt only. Base: go1.27.2 with P0-P5 and P6.
Requirements: A_17124-03 item 3, A_17094-02 (gemSpec_Krypt V2.51.0).
Upstream: never. Probe: K1.

